  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through next Friday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: AN upper level trough over the\nnorthwestern CONUS on Friday will drag a shortwave just to the\nnorth of the state by Saturday. While most of the effects of this\nsystem will remain north of the state, increased westerly wind\nflow in the base of the trough to the north will influence surface\nflow over northern NV Friday afternoon. \n\nSaturday stronger southerly flow over central NV will push wind\nspeeds to around 20 mph with gusts as high as 30 mph through\nSaturday afternoon. The parent trough to the north will begin to\ndrag a shortwave closer to the the western CONUS on Sunday. This\nshortwave will amplify and strengthen Sunday into Monday. By\nMonday morning a closed low will push across CA into southern NV. \n\nMoisture and vorticity advection in the downstream of the\nshortwave will create precipitation chances for eastern NV on\nMonday as PW values climb into the 0.5-0.6 inch range over\nnortheastern Nye, White Pine, and Elko Counties. Forcing with this\nsystem will be available mainly along the eastern border where \nLI's of 0 to -2 will be collocated with CAPE values up to 350 \nJ/kg. Storm activity is expected to be isolated with only highest \npeaks and ridges in White Pine County seeing any measurable \nrainfall. Ridging builds into the area by Tuesday night.\n\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: High confidence continues for\nfair weather conditions through the weekend. Low confidence exists\nin precipitation chances and amounts on Monday. No major grid\nedits needed at this time.",
